From d3e7f07ef7d6fe384ad3297c7d14f93ab82b3a4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iam <iam@iashur.internal>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 01:20:17 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] 360 viewer: brightness control (Touch controller A/B,
 keyboard b/d)

Multiplicative brightness on the displayed content: >1 brighter, <1 dimmer,
1.0 is native/off. Bound to the right Touch controller's A (up) and B (down)
buttons - the only real Touch inputs still free, since both thumbsticks
already carry seek (X) and zoom (Y). A/B only exist on the right Touch
controller (left has X/Y instead) and don't exist at all on
microsoft/motion_controller, so this is oculus/touch_controller-only,
edge-triggered like recenter/quit (fires once per press via
changedSinceLastSync, not repeatedly while held). Keyboard: b/d (brighter/
dimmer), 9 resets to 1x - pairs with 1 (normal speed) and 0 (normal zoom).

Threaded through panoFov.w, the last unused push-constant slot (x/y were
already half-angles/half-extents, z is zoom) - still no push-constant
growth. frag.glsl multiplies FragColor.rgb by it right after the texture
sample, before the progress-bar/quit-hold overlay bars, so dimming the
video never also dims that feedback.

Verified: keyboard sequence via fake pty (up x3/down x1/reset -> 1.15 ->
1.32 -> 1.52 -> 1.32 -> 1.00x, matching zoom's pattern exactly), and the
action registers correctly against real hardware ("BrightnessUp action is
bound to 'Right Oculus Touch Controller A'", no collision with anything).
CONFIRMED live with the headset on: user pressed A/B during actual
playback, "funciona bien, sube y baja el brillo".
